description: No IDE/tooling attribution in product docs, commits, or PRs
alwaysApply: true
---

# Delivery voice

Product codebases must read as the team’s work — not as an IDE or AI-editor showcase.

## Never put in product delivery artifacts

Do **not** mention Cursor (or “made / generated / co-authored with” Cursor or similar IDE/AI-editor branding) in:

- README and other repo documentation written for the product/codebase
- `docs/` that ship with the app (including product-facing `docs/sdlc` notes meant for the repo history)
- Commit messages and git trailers (`Co-authored-by`, “Generated with …”, etc.)
- Pull request titles/bodies, push notes, release notes, and changelogs

## Prefer

- Neutral, tool-agnostic wording when process must be described (“isolated review task”, “workspace apply”, “agent handoff”).
- Commit and PR text that explains the product change only.

## Exception

The **Matrix kit** source tree may name the IDE in install/setup/constitution docs that teach how to run m4tr!x. That exception does **not** apply to product apps the kit is applied onto.
